A **Poolside** water surface as a #C#Godot 4# spatial shader! Put it on a plane (a `PlaneMesh` in Godot, or **Add, Plane** in [Zonerider](https://radii-office.com/zonerider/)) and it shimmers by itself.

* `deep` and `shallow` are the two blues of the water
* `glint` is the warm orange of sunlight on the ripples
* `speed` and `scale` change how fast and how big the caustics are

In Zonerider, select the plane and, in its **Godot shader** section, choose **Open .gdshader…** and pick `poolside_water.gdshader`! Fork this lite to make your own colors!

~~~ file: poolside_water.gdshader
shader_type spatial;
render_mode specular_schlick_ggx;

uniform vec4 deep : source_color = vec4(0.02, 0.36, 0.72, 1.0);
uniform vec4 shallow : source_color = vec4(0.13, 0.83, 0.93, 1.0);
uniform vec4 glint : source_color = vec4(0.98, 0.57, 0.24, 1.0);
uniform float speed : hint_range(0.0, 3.0) = 0.6;
uniform float scale : hint_range(1.0, 20.0) = 6.0;

// soft cells that drift: the bright lines between them look like pool caustics
float caustic(vec2 p, float t) {
	vec2 i = floor(p);
	vec2 f = fract(p);
	float best = 1.0;
	for (int y = -1; y <= 1; y++) {
		for (int x = -1; x <= 1; x++) {
			vec2 g = vec2(float(x), float(y));
			vec2 o = fract(sin(vec2(dot(i + g, vec2(127.1, 311.7)), dot(i + g, vec2(269.5, 183.3)))) * 43758.5453);
			o = 0.5 + 0.5 * sin(t + 6.2831 * o);
			best = min(best, length(g + o - f));
		}
	}
	return best;
}

void fragment() {
	float t = TIME * speed;
	float c = caustic(UV * scale, t);
	float lines = pow(1.0 - c, 6.0);
	vec3 water = mix(deep.rgb, shallow.rgb, smoothstep(0.0, 0.9, UV.y + 0.15 * sin(t + UV.x * 4.0)));
	ALBEDO = water + lines * 0.55;
	EMISSION = glint.rgb * smoothstep(0.82, 1.0, lines) * 0.9;
	ROUGHNESS = 0.08;
	METALLIC = 0.0;
	SPECULAR = 0.7;
}
~~~

~~~ file: README.kd
# Poolside water

A Godot 4 spatial shader, public domain (CC0)!

* Godot: make a ShaderMaterial, load poolside_water.gdshader, and set it on a PlaneMesh
* Zonerider: select the plane, then Godot shader, Open .gdshader
* Colors: cyan and blue water, orange glints
~~~
